e automation identity while retaining both explicit ids. The same C22 cycle then read a safe, explicit REVISE but quarantined it because negative manifest evidence mentioning no added or removed files was misclassified as destructive. Controller 94 / Skill revision 2026-08-13.49 narrows that gate to ignore only explicit absence/not-proven evidence while preserving real destructive-action blocking. C23 proved the real one-shot wait, gated browser read, slot release, and deletion, but its safe boundary saying release/delete/resume was not approved was still quarantined. Controller 95 / Skill revision 2026-08-13.50 accepts that explicit non-approval boundary while preserving affirmative high-impact blocking. C24 sent exactly once and captured the real request identity, but the required same-task guard before confirmation rotated its valid send lease. Controller 96 / Skill revision 2026-08-13.51 preserves an authorized send lease across same-task guards until receipt confirmation while retaining normal orphan rotation and cross-task exclusion. C25 then completed one real scheduled wait, paired and consumed the unique reply, deleted the wait, and released the account slot without coordinator prompting; its next same-task guard was blocked because the waiting occurrence still held a review_poll lease. Controller 97 / Skill revision 2026-08-13.52 atomically hands that validated lease to apply_result so the same task may continue implementation while unrelated active leases remain protected. C26 proved one unique send, one gated reply read, staging, slot release, and platform-wait deletion, but its generated waiting prompt abbreviated resume-from-reply as resume; the wrong subcommand failed closed and left the staged reply waiting. Controller 98 / Skill revision 2026-08-13.53 now renders the exact resume-from-reply command contract and required deletion-proof arguments. C27 completed three real isolated macOS web-review rounds with three unique submissions, three gated reads, three staged identities, three deleted one-shot waits, three single consumptions, zero coordinator follow-ups, and final completed state. Local repository coverage is 287 including deterministic release packaging; Controller 98 passed all six Windows, macOS, and Ubuntu Python 3.11/3.13 jobs. C28 then attempted a real UNSEEN project run but stopped at 0/3 before state or Chat creation after misclassifying a completed composer fill with enabled send control as unresponsive; revision 2026-08-13.54 fixes that execution rule locally. C29 then initialized and named one Extreme reviewer Chat and completed its first verified UNSEEN diff, but stopped at 0/3 after inventing a Git commit prerequisite whose external worktree index required approval; revision 2026-08-13.55 makes verified worktree evidence sufficient unless commit identity is explicitly required. The frozen release gate remains zero because C27 used an isolated fixture and C28 completed no formal real-project cycle. Host enforcement, ten consecutive clean real project cycles, the macOS browser matrix, and real network/rate-limit recovery remain Beta blockers.",
